<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21276] sanityn test_39a/39d: mtime is not updated on write</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21276</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanityn test_39a and test_39d intermittently fail with "mtime is not updated on write". They read date +%s, write, read date +%s again, and require d1 &amp;lt;= mtime &amp;lt;= d2. That fails when the kernel timestamp falls just outside the userspace window.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the same kernel vs. userspace clock skew that b6242fd0f9ce ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12105" title="sanity test 39c fails with ''mtime is not updated on write: N &amp;lt;= (N - 1) &amp;lt;= N" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12105"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12105&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: fix sanity/39 checks and style") fixed in sanity.sh test_39c/39l. That patch didn't touch sanityn.sh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: the same as &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12105" title="sanity test 39c fails with ''mtime is not updated on write: N &amp;lt;= (N - 1) &amp;lt;= N" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12105"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12105&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, a sleep 0.5 before and after the write.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;distro/arch&amp;gt;</environment>
